// Module `import` grammar and namespace-lowering rung.
//
// `import "URI" as name ;` is recognized by the PBG grammar and retained by
// surface lowering. `as name` qualifies the import through the namespace
// engine. The URI remains a plain string literal, so new schemes need no
// grammar change: `file:///` today, others later. Resolution, signatures, and
// the wider module system remain separate from this declaration boundary.

import "file:///lib/prelude.gandr" as prelude ;

import "file:///lib/list.gandr" as list_ext ;
